think r1 (amphora) and r2 (comlink guests) proved the discipline on a small module and a large uniform cluster. r3 takes the three Q-vane voice modules — lattice, ember, lantern — READMEs and authored .rye/.rish prose. Unlike the comlink guests these are non-uniform: a version ordinal in a header, a /// function-doc lap prefix, a long fixtures table.
think Scoped r3 to lattice + ember + lantern (a natural semantic group — the Q-vane's tensor, craft, and inference voices), leaving mandi · greencandy · glow/nock for r4. 38 sites: 9 hand-judged prose sites + lantern/README.md's 29-row fixtures table.
think The 29-row lantern table maps each fixture file to what it pins, prefixed "Lap N" (provenance). The description column already carries each fixture's purpose, so the "Lap N" is pure drift — a sed dropped the prefix, each fixture kept by its own purpose (pinned completion · long completion · model-hash allow-list …). Residual 0 by an independent grep after.
think The 9 hand sites relabeled meaning-first: (lap 39)/(lap 33) version tags → semantic name + git stamp; "Lantern lap 33 selftest" → "Lantern selftest · 20260713"; "/// Lap 1: return fixture completion" → "/// Return fixture completion"; lattice README's "lap 31 minimum · … Inference lap 1 close" → "minimum tensor set · … Inference arc close"; ember's "Lap 2 deepens filters" → "Filters deepened · 20260809", "Lap 0 catalogs" → "The catalog folds".
obs Comment-only + README changes — zero code tokens moved. Proven safe on metal: buhr_inference_query (builds Lattice+Lantern) GREEN, buhr_reading_query (Scribble+Lantern) GREEN, gism_j5_corpus_real_ember (builds ember_core) GREEN. A raw-shell rye build fails only for lack of zig on PATH; the witness harness sets it up and passes.
